From 907d09c9f6bae726016c15ba851d39b5a992428f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:07:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] placement: $HOME/${HOME} and home-relative .hermes
 paths are state-path markers

PR #2405 review 5894942332 nit (pre-existing on main): HERMES_STATE_PATH knew only the
`~/` and `/home/<u>/` prefixes, so card bodies like `cat $HOME/.hermes/.env`,
`cat "${HOME}"/.hermes/auth.json` or `cd ~ && cat .hermes/.env` never matched the
state-path home marker and could be placed anywhere. Misplacement only: hub-read still
enforces its own READ_ROOTS.

- kanban_placement.HOME_PREFIX adds `$HOME`, `${HOME}` and their double-quoted forms.
- HERMES_STATE_PATH also matches a relative `.hermes/<x>` after a `cd` to home (`cd`,
  `cd ~`, `cd $HOME`, `cd /home/<u>`, quoted forms) anywhere earlier in the text. A later
  `cd` elsewhere is not tracked, so such text still pins (fails toward the home gateway).
  The code-checkout exclusions (hermes-agent, repos, bin) are unchanged.
- kanban_home_marker_placement._state_path uses HOME_PREFIX, so a pool worker still
  probes `$HOME/.hermes/kanban/workspaces/<t>` artifacts it holds (a-artifact keep).
- hub-read root clearing (`_strip_read_paths`, `_STATE_PATH`) is unchanged and only
  clears `~`/`/home/<u>` paths, so a declared hub:read never clears the new forms; tests
  pin that.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_state_path_home_forms.py (new, 31 RED on
origin/main, GREEN here) and the a-artifact keep test parametrized over `~`, `$HOME`,
`${HOME}` in test_kanban_pool_queue.py. New file, not rows in
test_kanban_hub_read_roots.py, to avoid conflicting with open PR #2405's hunks there.
